1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,490
More than ten thousand dollars.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:04,730
That's how much you can now save
on one brand-new ute in Australia,

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:06,550
compared with its old list price.

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,910
Not a used car.

5
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,550
Not a demo with forty
thousand kilometres on it.

6
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,550
A new ute, from one of the
biggest car brands in the country.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,050
And the reason is brutal.

8
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,230
When this ute launched,

9
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,630
the brand was talking about selling
twenty thousand a year in Australia.

10
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,590
In the first nine months of 2026,
it sold fewer than four hundred.

11
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,870
It's not the only one.

12
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:28,874
Right now, you can buy a brand-new
car for under twenty thousand dollars

13
00:00:28,924 --> 00:00:29,330
drive-away.

14
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:33,090
Toyota a brand that almost never discounts
is offering four thousand dollars

15
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,650
on the HiLux.

16
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,890
Ford is offering five
thousand on the Ranger.

17
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:40,650
And Black Friday deals are landing on
cars that used to have waiting lists.

18
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,630
So in this video,

19
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:45,090
I'm counting down the ten biggest
new-car deals in Australia right now,

20
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,770
from smallest to biggest.

21
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:49,150
Real offers, from the brands
and the motoring press,

22
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,150
with the prices, the end
dates and the catches,

23
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,170
because almost every one
of these deals has one.

24
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:55,950
Stay to the end,

25
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,110
because number one is the deal that tells
you the most about where this market

26
00:00:59,160 --> 00:00:59,960
is heading.

27
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:02,849
First, why is this happening now?

28
00:01:02,899 --> 00:01:08,889
Australians bought 107,493
new vehicles in October 2026,

29
00:01:08,939 --> 00:01:10,229
a record for the month.

30
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:11,409
So people are buying.

31
00:01:11,459 --> 00:01:14,329
But they're buying very different
cars from even a year ago.

32
00:01:14,379 --> 00:01:19,009
Electric car sales were up 237
per cent on October last year,

33
00:01:19,059 --> 00:01:21,909
BYD sold more than ten thousand
cars in a single month,

34
00:01:21,959 --> 00:01:24,849
and cars built in China
were up 104 per cent.

35
00:01:24,899 --> 00:01:28,549
That means a lot of brands are sitting
on stock they can't move especially

36
00:01:28,599 --> 00:01:31,509
utes, big SUVs and older models.

37
00:01:31,559 --> 00:01:34,039
Mitsubishi sales were down
50 per cent in October.

38
00:01:34,089 --> 00:01:36,189
Renault was down 58 per cent.

39
00:01:36,239 --> 00:01:38,509
Hyundai was down almost 29.

40
00:01:38,559 --> 00:01:42,229
Even Ford, the maker of Australia's
favourite ute, was down 3 per cent.

41
00:01:42,279 --> 00:01:43,769
And there's a second pressure.

42
00:01:43,819 --> 00:01:45,149
It's the end of the year.

43
00:01:45,199 --> 00:01:46,869
Dealers have annual targets,

44
00:01:46,919 --> 00:01:52,029
factories want to clear 2025 and 2026-built
cars before the new plates arrive,

45
00:01:52,079 --> 00:01:54,569
and Black Friday falls
on the 27th of November.

46
00:01:54,619 --> 00:01:58,149
So brands are throwing
everything at buyers price cuts,

47
00:01:58,199 --> 00:02:03,369
cashback, fuel cards, deposit contributions,
gift cards and free servicing.

48
00:02:03,419 --> 00:02:05,089
A quick note before we start.

49
00:02:05,139 --> 00:02:08,529
These deals are current
as of mid-November 2026.

50
00:02:08,579 --> 00:02:10,909
Most of them end on the 30th of November,

51
00:02:10,959 --> 00:02:14,249
the 21st of December or
the 31st of December.

52
00:02:14,299 --> 00:02:16,449
Drive-away prices can change by state,

53
00:02:16,499 --> 00:02:18,889
and some deals are only
for private buyers.

54
00:02:18,939 --> 00:02:21,349
So always get the final price
in writing from the dealer.

55
00:02:21,399 --> 00:02:22,559
Let's go.

56
00:02:23,352 --> 00:02:25,882
Number ten: the fuel card war.

57
00:02:25,932 --> 00:02:30,522
Some brands don't want to cut the
price, because that hurts resale values.

58
00:02:30,572 --> 00:02:32,782
So instead, they hand you a fuel card.

59
00:02:32,832 --> 00:02:36,662
Chery is offering a two-thousand-dollar
fuel card on the Tiggo 7,

60
00:02:36,712 --> 00:02:41,582
with the Tiggo 7 Urban
at $29,990 drive-away,

61
00:02:41,632 --> 00:02:44,542
and a fifteen-hundred-dollar
fuel card on the Tiggo 4,

62
00:02:44,592 --> 00:02:48,202
which starts at $23,990 drive-away.

63
00:02:48,252 --> 00:02:52,722
The Chery E5 electric SUV gets two
thousand dollars cashback instead.

64
00:02:52,772 --> 00:02:55,562
Those offers run until
the 21st of December,

65
00:02:55,612 --> 00:02:57,802
according to the deals tracker CarSorted.

66
00:02:57,852 --> 00:02:59,882
Mitsubishi is doing the same thing.

67
00:02:59,932 --> 00:03:02,622
There's a three-thousand-dollar
fuel card on the Triton ute,

68
00:03:02,672 --> 00:03:06,282
and a two-thousand-dollar fuel card
on the Outlander LS Black Edition,

69
00:03:06,332 --> 00:03:12,442
which is listed at $47,990
drive-away until the end of November.

70
00:03:12,492 --> 00:03:14,602
Now, here's the catch with fuel cards.

71
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:17,802
A two-thousand-dollar fuel card is not
the same as two thousand dollars off

72
00:03:17,852 --> 00:03:18,202
the price.

73
00:03:18,252 --> 00:03:20,462
You can't spend it on anything else,

74
00:03:20,512 --> 00:03:23,722
it doesn't reduce your loan, and
it doesn't reduce the stamp duty.

75
00:03:23,772 --> 00:03:25,362
If a dealer offers you a fuel card,

76
00:03:25,412 --> 00:03:29,082
it's always worth asking: could I
have that as a discount instead?

77
00:03:29,132 --> 00:03:30,422
Sometimes the answer is yes.

78
00:03:30,472 --> 00:03:32,322
And remember the context.

79
00:03:32,372 --> 00:03:34,622
Mitsubishi's sales halved in October.

80
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:36,502
When a brand's sales fall that far,

81
00:03:36,552 --> 00:03:39,632
there's usually more room to
negotiate than the advertised offer.

82
00:03:41,248 --> 00:03:42,329
Number nine: Honda's plate clearance.

83
00:03:42,379 --> 00:03:46,169
Honda sells its cars at fixed,
no-haggle prices in Australia.

84
00:03:46,219 --> 00:03:49,409
So instead of cutting the price,
it's giving away gift cards.

85
00:03:49,459 --> 00:03:52,389
Its end-of-year plate clearance,
reported by CarExpert,

86
00:03:52,439 --> 00:03:57,309
runs until the 31st of January
2027 on 2026-built cars.

87
00:03:57,359 --> 00:03:59,049
The biggest gift card is
three thousand dollars,

88
00:03:59,099 --> 00:04:04,689
on the CR-V e:HEV X hybrid
and the ZR-V e:HEV X hybrid.

89
00:04:04,739 --> 00:04:08,449
Other CR-V and ZR-V hybrids
get fifteen hundred dollars.

90
00:04:08,499 --> 00:04:12,989
And the Civic, the HR-V, the Prelude
and the Accord get a thousand dollars.

91
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:14,129
On top of that,

92
00:04:14,179 --> 00:04:17,729
Honda is throwing in the first five
scheduled services for free that's five

93
00:04:17,779 --> 00:04:19,869
years or fifty thousand kilometres.

94
00:04:19,919 --> 00:04:23,629
CarExpert valued that at $1,395.

95
00:04:23,679 --> 00:04:25,169
So on the best-value models,

96
00:04:25,219 --> 00:04:28,149
you're looking at around four
thousand dollars in total benefits.

97
00:04:28,199 --> 00:04:30,389
Not bad from a brand that
almost never does deals.

98
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:32,109
Here's the catch.

99
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:38,049
Honda's annual service price has
just gone up, from $199 to $279.

100
00:04:38,099 --> 00:04:41,649
So that free servicing is worth
more than it was a month ago.

101
00:04:41,699 --> 00:04:45,449
And remember, the gift card arrives
within thirty days of delivery it doesn't

102
00:04:45,499 --> 00:04:47,369
come off the price you pay on the day.

103
00:04:47,419 --> 00:04:48,989
And if you're thinking about the Accord,

104
00:04:49,039 --> 00:04:50,989
it was the number one
car in my last video,

105
00:04:51,039 --> 00:04:53,619
with just fifty-nine sold in nine months.

106
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:56,015
Number eight: GWM.

107
00:04:56,065 --> 00:04:58,835
GWM is a Chinese brand,

108
00:04:58,885 --> 00:05:02,315
but it's not riding the
Chinese boom like BYD or Geely.

109
00:05:02,365 --> 00:05:05,435
In October, GWM's sales
were basically flat,

110
00:05:05,485 --> 00:05:10,035
down 0.3 per cent the only Chinese brand
in the top ten that went backwards.

111
00:05:10,085 --> 00:05:11,855
And it's responding with deals.

112
00:05:11,905 --> 00:05:13,635
According to GWM's own offers,

113
00:05:13,685 --> 00:05:15,275
listed by CarSorted,

114
00:05:15,325 --> 00:05:20,335
the Haval Jolion Premium
Hybrid is $32,990 drive-away,

115
00:05:20,385 --> 00:05:22,855
with a three-thousand-dollar
deposit contribution.

116
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:28,275
The bigger Haval H6 Ultra
Hybrid is $43,990 drive-away,

117
00:05:28,325 --> 00:05:31,035
also with three thousand
dollars towards your deposit.

118
00:05:31,085 --> 00:05:36,655
The H6 Lux petrol is $35,990
drive-away with two thousand.

119
00:05:36,705 --> 00:05:40,795
And the Cannon ute is
from $39,990 drive-away,

120
00:05:40,845 --> 00:05:43,195
with a smaller
five-hundred-dollar contribution.

121
00:05:43,245 --> 00:05:45,535
All of those run until
the 30th of November.

122
00:05:45,585 --> 00:05:46,415
Back in October,

123
00:05:46,465 --> 00:05:51,735
CarExpert reported GWM offering up to
five thousand dollars off selected SUVs.

124
00:05:51,785 --> 00:05:53,835
So this brand is clearly in a hurry.

125
00:05:53,885 --> 00:05:54,655
The catch?

126
00:05:54,705 --> 00:05:57,295
A deposit contribution is
effectively a discount,

127
00:05:57,345 --> 00:06:00,455
but it's usually tied to
finance or to specific stock.

128
00:06:00,505 --> 00:06:03,315
And remember, these deals
change month to month.

129
00:06:03,365 --> 00:06:04,875
If you miss the end of November,

130
00:06:04,925 --> 00:06:07,915
there's a good chance another deal
turns up in December but there's no

131
00:06:07,965 --> 00:06:09,845
guarantee it will be the same one.

132
00:06:10,657 --> 00:06:13,247
Number seven: the Toyota HiLux.

133
00:06:13,297 --> 00:06:14,347
This one is rare.

134
00:06:14,397 --> 00:06:16,127
Toyota doesn't need to discount much,

135
00:06:16,177 --> 00:06:19,367
because Toyota sells more
cars than anyone in Australia.

136
00:06:19,417 --> 00:06:22,747
In October, the HiLux was the
best-selling vehicle in the country,

137
00:06:22,797 --> 00:06:25,627
with 5,954 sales.

138
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:27,787
But the ute market is getting crowded.

139
00:06:27,837 --> 00:06:29,327
So according to CarExpert,

140
00:06:29,377 --> 00:06:33,740
Toyota is offering a four-thousand-dollar
finance deposit bonus on HiLux SR5

141
00:06:33,790 --> 00:06:38,187
four-by-four dual-cab pickups and
cab-chassis models diesel only.

142
00:06:38,237 --> 00:06:39,157
With the bonus,

143
00:06:39,207 --> 00:06:45,327
CarExpert says the effective prices
before on-road costs are $59,990 for

144
00:06:45,377 --> 00:06:47,347
the manual dual-cab pickup,

145
00:06:47,397 --> 00:06:50,527
$60,490 for the automatic cab-chassis,

146
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:54,947
and $61,990 for the
automatic dual-cab pickup.

147
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:57,407
Now, here's the catch and it's a big one.

148
00:06:57,457 --> 00:07:00,167
You have to finance the
car through Toyota Finance,

149
00:07:00,217 --> 00:07:02,667
and you have to borrow at
least ten thousand dollars.

150
00:07:02,717 --> 00:07:03,767
Leases don't count.

151
00:07:03,817 --> 00:07:06,127
And the electric HiLux isn't included.

152
00:07:06,177 --> 00:07:10,127
You'll need to order and apply for
finance by the 31st of December,

153
00:07:10,177 --> 00:07:12,187
with settlement by the end of February.

154
00:07:12,237 --> 00:07:15,487
So if you were going to pay cash,
this deal isn't really for you.

155
00:07:15,537 --> 00:07:17,387
But if you were going to finance anyway,

156
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,707
compare Toyota's interest
rate with your bank's.

157
00:07:19,757 --> 00:07:23,167
A four-thousand-dollar bonus can
disappear quickly if the interest rate is

158
00:07:23,217 --> 00:07:24,017
higher.

159
00:07:24,493 --> 00:07:28,023
Number six: BYD's
four-thousand-dollar cashback.

160
00:07:28,073 --> 00:07:32,283
BYD is the second biggest brand in the
country and it's growing like crazy up

161
00:07:32,333 --> 00:07:34,983
153 per cent in October.

162
00:07:35,033 --> 00:07:36,743
So why is it offering cashback?

163
00:07:36,793 --> 00:07:38,103
Because it's in a price war,

164
00:07:38,153 --> 00:07:40,743
and it wants to keep the
pressure on everyone else.

165
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,343
According to CarExpert,

166
00:07:42,393 --> 00:07:46,243
BYD is offering four thousand
dollars cashback on the Seal 6,

167
00:07:46,293 --> 00:07:51,163
the Shark 6 ute and the
Sealion 5, 6, 7 and 8 SUVs.

168
00:07:51,213 --> 00:07:52,263
With the cashback,

169
00:07:52,313 --> 00:07:58,603
the Sealion 5 Essential works out
at $29,990 before on-road costs.

170
00:07:58,653 --> 00:08:02,563
The Sealion 7 Premium one of the
best-selling electric cars in the country

171
00:08:02,613 --> 00:08:05,163
works out at $50,990.

172
00:08:05,213 --> 00:08:09,903
And the Shark 6 Premium
plug-in hybrid ute is $53,900.

173
00:08:09,953 --> 00:08:14,263
There's also 0.99 per cent finance
over thirty-six months on most of those

174
00:08:14,313 --> 00:08:14,793
models.

175
00:08:14,843 --> 00:08:17,443
Orders have to be placed
by the 21st of December,

176
00:08:17,493 --> 00:08:19,643
with delivery by the end of the year.

177
00:08:19,693 --> 00:08:20,363
The catch?

178
00:08:20,413 --> 00:08:22,863
The cashback can't be combined
with other BYD offers,

179
00:08:22,913 --> 00:08:26,543
it's not for fleet buyers, and
demonstrators aren't included.

180
00:08:26,593 --> 00:08:30,103
And Zecar reported claims that some
dealers are adding another two thousand on

181
00:08:30,153 --> 00:08:32,563
top but BYD hasn't confirmed that.

182
00:08:32,613 --> 00:08:35,553
So if a dealer offers you six
thousand, get it in writing.

183
00:08:37,233 --> 00:08:38,582
Number five: the Renault Duster.

184
00:08:38,632 --> 00:08:42,662
The Duster is a small, tough SUV, and
you can get it with four-wheel drive.

185
00:08:42,712 --> 00:08:45,722
Now it's had up to five thousand
dollars cut from its price,

186
00:08:45,772 --> 00:08:47,262
according to Cars24,

187
00:08:47,312 --> 00:08:52,762
and the entry-level Evolution two-wheel
drive is now $29,990 drive-away

188
00:08:52,812 --> 00:08:53,882
nationwide.

189
00:08:53,932 --> 00:08:57,882
That's a real off-road-capable SUV
for under thirty thousand dollars

190
00:08:57,932 --> 00:08:58,302
drive-away.

191
00:08:58,352 --> 00:09:01,877
The four-wheel-drive versions are around
thirty-four to thirty-six thousand

192
00:09:01,927 --> 00:09:03,142
drive-away in New South Wales.

193
00:09:03,192 --> 00:09:07,282
The offer covers cars bought and delivered
between the 1st of November and the

194
00:09:07,332 --> 00:09:08,942
31st of December.

195
00:09:08,992 --> 00:09:09,862
Why the deal?

196
00:09:09,912 --> 00:09:10,802
Renault didn't say.

197
00:09:10,852 --> 00:09:12,282
But the sales figures do.

198
00:09:12,332 --> 00:09:16,902
In October, the whole Renault brand
sold just 164 cars in Australia,

199
00:09:16,952 --> 00:09:19,642
down 58 per cent on the
same month last year.

200
00:09:19,692 --> 00:09:23,962
The Arkana sold four, the Koleos
21, and the Kangoo van just two.

201
00:09:24,012 --> 00:09:24,662
The catch?

202
00:09:24,712 --> 00:09:26,862
The advertised price is
for Solid White only.

203
00:09:26,912 --> 00:09:30,002
Any other colour adds $850.

204
00:09:30,052 --> 00:09:33,342
And fleet, government and rental
buyers can't get the deal.

205
00:09:33,392 --> 00:09:35,502
Also think about the brand's future here.

206
00:09:35,552 --> 00:09:36,822
With sales this low,

207
00:09:36,872 --> 00:09:38,802
ask about the dealer network near you,

208
00:09:38,852 --> 00:09:41,552
servicing costs and parts
supply before you sign.

209
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,840
Number four: the Ford Ranger.

210
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:46,350
This is Australia's
other favourite vehicle.

211
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:49,330
The Ranger has been the best-selling
vehicle in the country for four months

212
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,050
this year.

213
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:51,910
But it's in a fight with the HiLux,

214
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:55,850
with BYD's Shark 6, and with
a wave of new Chinese utes.

215
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,470
So according to CarExpert,

216
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:00,990
Ford is offering a five-thousand-dollar
fuel card or a discount of the same

217
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:06,690
value on the 2026.5 model year
Ranger XLT, Wildtrak and Tremor.

218
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,770
For the newer 2027 versions
of the same models,

219
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,770
the offer is four thousand dollars.

220
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:16,810
And the Ranger Black Edition V6 dual-cab
pickup has a drive-away price of

221
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:17,870
$59,000.

222
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,330
Here's the smart move.

223
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:22,550
Ford's offer gives you a choice
between a fuel card and a discount.

224
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,590
Take the discount.

225
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:26,630
As I said earlier, a discount
reduces the price you pay,

226
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,870
the amount you borrow and the stamp duty.

227
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,570
A fuel card does none of that.

228
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:31,290
The catch?

229
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:34,130
CarExpert didn't publish an end
date for these Ranger offers,

230
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:35,830
so they could end at any time.

231
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:38,910
And the five-thousand-dollar
offer is on the older model year.

232
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:42,450
If you're buying to keep for a long
time, the model year matters less.

233
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:45,240
If you'll sell it in two or
three years, it can matter more.

234
00:10:46,721 --> 00:10:48,194
Number three: Suzuki's Black Friday sale.

235
00:10:48,244 --> 00:10:52,454
Suzuki is running a Black Friday sale
with ten per cent off the price of black

236
00:10:52,504 --> 00:10:53,214
cars.

237
00:10:53,264 --> 00:10:55,394
Yes, it only applies to black cars.

238
00:10:55,444 --> 00:10:57,694
The biggest saving,
according to CarExpert,

239
00:10:57,744 --> 00:11:01,174
is on the new e Vitara Ultra electric SUV:

240
00:11:01,224 --> 00:11:07,394
$5,774 off, bringing it
to $51,962 drive-away.

241
00:11:07,444 --> 00:11:11,894
The e Vitara Motion is $42,862 drive-away,

242
00:11:11,944 --> 00:11:14,674
a saving of $4,874.

243
00:11:14,724 --> 00:11:19,654
The Vitara Turbo hybrid
is $36,762 drive-away,

244
00:11:19,704 --> 00:11:22,494
saving $3,974.

245
00:11:22,544 --> 00:11:25,254
And here's the one that'll
get attention: the Jimny.

246
00:11:25,304 --> 00:11:30,054
The three-door Jimny in
black is $35,762 drive-away,

247
00:11:30,104 --> 00:11:32,954
a saving of $3,474.

248
00:11:33,004 --> 00:11:37,954
The five-door Jimny XL
is $37,562 drive-away,

249
00:11:38,004 --> 00:11:40,534
saving $3,674.

250
00:11:40,584 --> 00:11:44,434
The Swift Hybrid starts
at $23,022 drive-away.

251
00:11:44,484 --> 00:11:46,314
The catches are important on this one.

252
00:11:46,364 --> 00:11:47,874
It's for private buyers only.

253
00:11:47,924 --> 00:11:51,154
You have to buy and take
delivery by the 30th of November.

254
00:11:51,204 --> 00:11:55,204
It only covers selected new and
demonstrator stock at participating dealers.

255
00:11:55,254 --> 00:11:58,774
Cars with a black roof and a
different body colour don't count,

256
00:11:58,824 --> 00:12:02,354
the Jimny Heritage isn't included
and the offer excludes Queensland and

257
00:12:02,404 --> 00:12:03,814
northern New South Wales.

258
00:12:03,864 --> 00:12:05,544
So if you're in Brisbane, sorry.

259
00:12:07,209 --> 00:12:09,561
Number two: the cheapest
new car in Australia.

260
00:12:09,611 --> 00:12:14,881
The BYD Atto 1 Essential
is now $19,990 drive-away.

261
00:12:14,931 --> 00:12:15,701
That's a brand-new,

262
00:12:15,751 --> 00:12:19,871
fully electric small car for under
twenty thousand dollars, on the road.

263
00:12:19,921 --> 00:12:22,701
Zecar describes it as
Australia's cheapest new car,

264
00:12:22,751 --> 00:12:28,861
and says the saving is
between $5,772 and $7,204,

265
00:12:28,911 --> 00:12:30,521
depending on your state.

266
00:12:30,571 --> 00:12:33,041
The offer runs for orders
until the 15th of December,

267
00:12:33,091 --> 00:12:35,941
with delivery by the 31st of December.

268
00:12:35,991 --> 00:12:41,081
BYD is also offering the Dolphin
Essential electric hatch at $28,888

269
00:12:41,131 --> 00:12:47,261
drive-away, and the Atto 2 plug-in
hybrid at $25,990 drive-away.

270
00:12:47,311 --> 00:12:48,721
Think about what that means.

271
00:12:48,771 --> 00:12:53,061
For years, the cheapest new cars in
Australia were small petrol hatchbacks.

272
00:12:53,111 --> 00:12:54,341
Now, according to Zecar,

273
00:12:54,391 --> 00:12:58,441
the cheapest new car you can buy is
electric, and it's made in China.

274
00:12:58,491 --> 00:12:59,181
The catch?

275
00:12:59,231 --> 00:13:01,361
The Atto 1 is a small city car.

276
00:13:01,411 --> 00:13:02,441
It's not a family SUV,

277
00:13:02,491 --> 00:13:06,961
and its range and space are built for
the city, not for long country drives.

278
00:13:07,011 --> 00:13:10,721
If most of your driving is in town,
it could save you a fortune in fuel.

279
00:13:10,771 --> 00:13:13,681
If you regularly drive hundreds
of kilometres in one go,

280
00:13:13,731 --> 00:13:15,471
test it properly before you sign.

281
00:13:16,223 --> 00:13:18,513
And number one: the Kia Tasman.

282
00:13:18,563 --> 00:13:20,493
The Tasman is Kia's first-ever ute,

283
00:13:20,543 --> 00:13:23,093
and it was developed
with Australia in mind.

284
00:13:23,143 --> 00:13:24,233
When it was announced,

285
00:13:24,283 --> 00:13:27,813
Kia was talking about a target of
around twenty thousand sales a year.

286
00:13:27,863 --> 00:13:29,253
But according to reports,

287
00:13:29,303 --> 00:13:33,933
fewer than four hundred Tasmans were
sold in the first nine months of 2026.

288
00:13:33,983 --> 00:13:35,853
So now Kia is cutting hard.

289
00:13:35,903 --> 00:13:38,433
According to a report published
on the 4th of November,

290
00:13:38,483 --> 00:13:45,233
the 2025-model Tasman SX four-wheel
drive is now $49,990 drive-away.

291
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:50,313
Its list price was $54,490
before on-road costs,

292
00:13:50,363 --> 00:13:52,513
so that's around five
thousand dollars off.

293
00:13:52,563 --> 00:13:58,093
And the Tasman SX+ four-wheel
drive is now $54,990 drive-away,

294
00:13:58,143 --> 00:14:02,733
down from $62,390 before on-road costs.

295
00:14:02,783 --> 00:14:05,453
Once you add in the on-road
costs you'd normally pay,

296
00:14:05,503 --> 00:14:07,893
that's a saving of more
than ten thousand dollars.

297
00:14:07,943 --> 00:14:12,113
ABN holders can also get five thousand
dollars off single and dual cab-chassis

298
00:14:12,163 --> 00:14:15,033
S and SX models with an alloy tray.

299
00:14:15,083 --> 00:14:15,873
The catch?

300
00:14:15,923 --> 00:14:18,973
The deal is only on 2025 model-year cars,

301
00:14:19,023 --> 00:14:21,593
and you have to order and
take delivery in November.

302
00:14:21,643 --> 00:14:23,093
So stock is limited.

303
00:14:23,143 --> 00:14:26,133
And with sales this low,
think about resale value.

304
00:14:26,183 --> 00:14:29,693
A ute with a small fan base is
harder to sell in a few years' time,

305
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:33,253
so plan to keep it for a while or make
sure the discount is big enough to

306
00:14:33,303 --> 00:14:34,823
cover the extra depreciation.

307
00:14:35,817 --> 00:14:37,767
Before we finish, a bonus.

308
00:14:37,817 --> 00:14:40,957
This isn't a runout deal, but it's
the biggest price cut I found.

309
00:14:41,007 --> 00:14:46,447
Audi has cut the price of the updated
Q4 e-tron electric SUV by up to eighteen

310
00:14:46,497 --> 00:14:47,227
thousand dollars.

311
00:14:47,277 --> 00:14:49,007
According to Cars24,

312
00:14:49,057 --> 00:14:54,207
the entry models are now
$71,650 before on-road costs,

313
00:14:54,257 --> 00:14:56,147
about thirteen thousand dollars cheaper,

314
00:14:56,197 --> 00:14:59,447
and the all-wheel-drive quattro versions
are up to eighteen thousand dollars

315
00:14:59,497 --> 00:15:00,407
cheaper.

316
00:15:00,457 --> 00:15:03,387
That brings them well under
the luxury car tax threshold.

317
00:15:03,437 --> 00:15:04,007
Why?

318
00:15:04,057 --> 00:15:08,427
Because the current Q4 e-tron sold
just two cars in Australia in October,

319
00:15:08,477 --> 00:15:09,707
down 96 per cent.

320
00:15:09,757 --> 00:15:13,807
The catch is that deliveries of the
updated model don't start until the first

321
00:15:13,857 --> 00:15:15,337
half of 2027.

322
00:15:16,178 --> 00:15:18,308
So how do you get the
best out of these deals?

323
00:15:18,358 --> 00:15:20,248
First, read the fine print.

324
00:15:20,298 --> 00:15:22,508
Look for words like "private buyers only",

325
00:15:22,558 --> 00:15:25,008
"selected stock", "participating dealers",

326
00:15:25,058 --> 00:15:28,248
"not combinable with other offers"
and "must be delivered by".

327
00:15:28,298 --> 00:15:31,008
Most of these deals end
on the 30th of November,

328
00:15:31,058 --> 00:15:34,308
the 21st of December or
the 31st of December.

329
00:15:34,358 --> 00:15:39,028
Second, always ask for a final drive-away
price in writing, for your postcode.

330
00:15:39,078 --> 00:15:41,228
Advertised prices can change by state.

331
00:15:41,278 --> 00:15:45,088
Third, prefer a real discount
over a fuel card or a gift card.

332
00:15:45,138 --> 00:15:48,268
A discount reduces what you
borrow and the stamp duty.

333
00:15:48,318 --> 00:15:50,608
Fourth, if a deal depends on finance,

334
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:54,948
compare the interest rate and the total
cost of the loan, not just the bonus.

335
00:15:54,998 --> 00:15:57,108
Fifth, ask about demonstrators.

336
00:15:57,158 --> 00:16:00,548
Several of these deals, like
Suzuki's, include demo stock.

337
00:16:00,598 --> 00:16:03,708
A demonstrator with a few thousand
kilometres can take another chunk off the

338
00:16:03,758 --> 00:16:07,628
price, and it's usually still covered
by most of the new-car warranty.

339
00:16:07,678 --> 00:16:08,988
Just check the build date,

340
00:16:09,038 --> 00:16:10,328
the date the warranty started,

341
00:16:10,378 --> 00:16:13,928
and the service history, and make
sure the price reflects any wear.

342
00:16:13,978 --> 00:16:15,568
Sixth, timing.

343
00:16:15,618 --> 00:16:16,848
The last week of a month,

344
00:16:16,898 --> 00:16:18,728
and especially the last weeks of December,

345
00:16:18,778 --> 00:16:21,568
is when dealers are most
desperate to hit their targets.

346
00:16:21,618 --> 00:16:23,788
If a deal ends on the 30th of November,

347
00:16:23,838 --> 00:16:26,908
don't be surprised if a new one
starts on the 1st of December.

348
00:16:26,958 --> 00:16:30,728
But don't wait too long on limited
stock once the cheap cars are gone,

349
00:16:30,778 --> 00:16:31,508
they're gone.

350
00:16:31,558 --> 00:16:33,608
And finally, think about resale.

351
00:16:33,658 --> 00:16:36,588
The biggest discounts are usually
on the cars that aren't selling.

352
00:16:36,638 --> 00:16:38,448
That's great for the price you pay today,

353
00:16:38,498 --> 00:16:40,488
but it can mean faster depreciation later.

354
00:16:40,538 --> 00:16:41,598
So that's the list:

355
00:16:41,648 --> 00:16:44,028
Chery and Mitsubishi's fuel cards,

356
00:16:44,078 --> 00:16:47,548
Honda's gift cards, GWM, the Toyota HiLux,

357
00:16:47,598 --> 00:16:50,028
BYD's cashback, the Renault Duster,

358
00:16:50,078 --> 00:16:52,908
the Ford Ranger, Suzuki's
Black Friday sale,

359
00:16:52,958 --> 00:16:56,808
the BYD Atto 1 under twenty
thousand dollars and at number one,

360
00:16:56,858 --> 00:16:59,808
the Kia Tasman, with more
than ten thousand dollars off.

361
00:16:59,858 --> 00:17:03,088
Now tell me in the comments: which of
these deals would you actually take?

362
00:17:03,138 --> 00:17:05,448
And if you've been offered a
better deal at a dealership,

363
00:17:05,498 --> 00:17:07,928
share it below, because
it'll help other buyers.

364
00:17:07,978 --> 00:17:08,988
If this video helped,

365
00:17:09,038 --> 00:17:12,668
hit like and subscribe and share it
with anyone who's about to buy a new car

366
00:17:12,718 --> 00:17:13,808
before Christmas.

367
00:17:13,858 --> 00:17:15,038
See you in the next one.
